From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:00:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rasapi32: phone book file (rasphone.pbk), credentials,
 autodial, connection notifications

Phone-book edits now work on the file Windows keeps them in:
%APPDATA%\Microsoft\Network\Connections\Pbk\rasphone.pbk (the user's) and the
all-users one under %ProgramData% (administrators only, else ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED).
- RasSetEntryProperties / RasGetEntryProperties (A and W, any structure size from
  Windows 95's to Vista's), RasValidateEntryName, RasDeleteEntry, RasRenameEntry,
  RasSetEntryDialParams / RasGetEntryDialParams (user, domain, phone, callback;
  the password protected with CryptProtectData), RasSetCredentials / new
  RasGetCredentials, RasSetCustomAuthData, RasSetSubEntryProperties / new
  RasGetSubEntryProperties, RasDeleteSubEntry.
- RasEnumEntries lists the phone-book entries beside the VPN connections.
- RasCreatePhonebookEntry / RasEditPhonebookEntry show a small dialog (name, phone
  number, device) that writes the entry.
- RasSet/Get/EnumAutodial*: addresses, enable flags and parameters under
  HKCU\Software\Microsoft\RAS AutoDial.
- RasConnectionNotification: a thread polls the VPN connections (sg-netctl) and
  signals the registered events on connect and disconnect.
- RasHangUp without sg-netctl is ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE (no connection exists).
Dialling stays the VPN connections' only (the documented error otherwise).

Gate: test/fastrasbook-gate.sh (64/32; scratch prefix, stand-in sg-netctl).
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
